guid":"-Zj9KumBgLHMvOqmnJ9W_w","children":[{"id":"136","parent":"135","text":"Estrategia de tratamiento mas adecuada","guid":"mE9Ar-r5D1GiQbKI5jLLKA","children":[]},{"id":"137","parent":"135","text":"Modificar prioridades a lo largo del tiempo de\\Nacuerdo a la evolución del paciente","guid":"MZdg09LpcpCPvyu-6vdrSA","children":[]}]}]}]},{"id":"138","parent":"0","text":"Perlas Clínicas","guid":"7C47EFD89AA44F02A3716E91","children":[{"id":"139","parent":"138","text":"VENTANA DE NEUROPLASTICIDAD MÁXIMA POST-ACV: PRIMEROS 3 MESES → INTENSIFICAR REHABILITACIÓN PRECOZ Y DOSIS-DEPENDIENTE; CADA HORA ADICIONAL DE TERAPIA MEJORA OUTCOMES (META-ANÁLISIS LOHSE 2014)","guid":"4407BA7EA7254805991E18D0","children":[]},{"id":"140","parent":"138","text":"MOVILIZACIÓN PRECOZ DEBE INICIARSE EN 24-48 H SI HEMODINÁMICAMENTE ESTABLE → AVERT TRIAL: MOVILIZACIÓN MUY PRECOZ Y FRECUENTE (<24 H) FUE INFERIOR A USUAL CARE; PREFERIR MOVILIZACIÓN DOSIS-MODERADA","guid":"943DF304D66744BEBC420259","children":[]},{"id":"141","parent":"138","text":"TERAPIA DE RESTRICCIÓN INDUCIDA (CIMT) PARA EXTREMIDAD SUPERIOR: 6 H/DÍA × 2 SEM CON RESTRICCIÓN DEL BRAZO SANO; EVIDENCIA NIVEL 1A; SELECCIÓN: PACIENTE CON EXTENSIÓN ACTIVA DE 10° EN MUÑECA Y 10° EN DEDOS","guid":"27E368E382CA4DB1B4F202C0","children":[]},{"id":"142","parent":"138","text":"ESTIMULACIÓN ELÉCTRICA FUNCIONAL EN ESPÁSTICOS REDUCE PIE EQUINO Y MEJORA VELOCIDAD DE MARCHA; ROBÓTICA + TERAPIA CONVENCIONAL > TERAPIA SOLA EN MARCHA POST-ACV (META-ANÁLISIS COCHRANE 2020)","guid":"5884E814659E45BFA6166F13","children":[]},{"id":"143","parent":"138","text":"DISFAGIA POST-ACV AFECTA AL 50% INICIALMENTE; SCREENING CON GUSS O TEST DE AGUA EN 4-24 H POST-INGRESO; SI POSITIVO → VFC O FEES; SNG SI NPO >7 DÍAS, GASTROSTOMÍA SI >4 SEM","guid":"BF6941595B25419A92C0E5EC","children":[]},{"id":"144","parent":"138","text":"TROMBOPROFILAXIS: HBPM PROFILÁCTICA EN ACV ISQUÉMICO 24 H POST-INGRESO; EN HEMORRÁGICO ESPERAR 48-72 H + COMPRESIÓN NEUMÁTICA INTERMITENTE DESDE EL DÍA 1 (CLOTS-3)","guid":"DC0BB35E52944F5A9F81FFCC","children":[]},{"id":"145","parent":"138","text":"ESPASTICIDAD: TRATAMIENTO ESCALONADO → POSICIONAMIENTO + ESTIRAMIENTO → BACLOFENO ORAL → TOXINA BOTULÍNICA INTRAMUSCULAR (PRIMERA LÍNEA EN ESPASTICIDAD FOCAL); REPETIR CADA 3-4 MESES","guid":"A8F08D0D908B48D58592670D","children":[]},{"id":"146","parent":"138","text":"DEPRESIÓN POST-ACV PREVALENCIA 30% A 1 AÑO → SCREENING CON PHQ-9; ISRS (SERTRALINA, FLUOXETINA) MEJORAN ESTADO DE ÁNIMO PERO FLUOXETINA NO MEJORA RECUPERACIÓN MOTORA (FOCUS, AFFINITY, EFFECTS TRIALS)","guid":"2869B2338F37450F9A13B012","children":[]},{"id":"147","parent":"138","text":"ESCALAS DE OUTCOME: NIHSS (BASAL Y SEGUIMIENTO), BARTHEL (ABVD), FUGL-MEYER (FUNCIÓN MOTORA), MoCA (COGNICIÓN), MRS (DISCAPACIDAD GLOBAL); MEDIR AL INGRESO + 3 + 6 MESES","guid":"BD26066FFC2C4EF7832ECDA1","children":[]},{"id":"148","parent":"138","text":"ALTA HOSPITALARIA REQUIERE ENTRENAMIENTO DEL CUIDADOR + ADAPTACIONES DOMICILIARIAS; PROGRAMAS DE TELE-REHABILITACIÓN NO INFERIORES A PRESENCIAL EN MARCHA Y EXTREMIDAD SUPERIOR (META-ANÁLISIS 2023)","guid":"BCC0CE08384B4921BC266DE7","children":[]},{"id":"149","parent":"138","text":"Referencias","guid":"6D549E05328B4835AE437D26","children":[{"id":"150","parent":"149","text":"1. Winstein CJ, Stein J, Arena R, et al. Guidelines for adult stroke rehabilitation and recovery: a guideline for healthcare professionals from the AHA/ASA. Stroke. 2016;47(6):e98-169.","guid":"78FD0FB3E9E04C8791726F90","children":[]},{"id":"151","parent":"149","text":"2. AVERT Trial Collaboration Group. Efficacy and safety of very early mobilisation within 24 h of stroke onset (AVERT): a randomised controlled trial. Lancet. 2015;386(9988):46-55.","guid":"CE7C30EE95514D08A024862C","children":[]},{"id":"152","parent":"149","text":"3. Wolf SL, Winstein CJ, Miller JP, et al. Effect of constraint-induced movement therapy on upper extremity function 3 to 9 months after stroke (EXCITE). JAMA. 2006;296(17):2095-104.","guid":"9D9E2183FAE94083AC85AC19","children":[]},{"id":"153","parent":"149","text":"4. Mehrholz J, Thomas S, Werner C, et al. Electromechanical-assisted training for walking after stroke. Cochrane Database Syst Rev. 2020;10:CD006185.","guid":"14A2AC629E7B4D05BE030176","children":[]},{"id":"154","parent":"149","text":"5. Dennis M, Sandercock P, Reid J, et al. Effectiveness of intermittent pneumatic compression in reduction of risk of DVT in patients with stroke (CLOTS 3). Lancet. 2013;382(9891):516-24.","guid":"7C48327C1D2941EFADD22CE7","children":[]},{"id":"155","parent":"149","text":"6. Dennis M, Mead G, Forbes J, et al. Effects of fluoxetine on functional outcomes after acute stroke (FOCUS): a pragmatic, double-blind, randomised, controlled trial. Lancet. 2019;393(10168):265-74.","guid":"24D003435CF7423CAEE6CC93","children":[]},{"id":"156","parent":"149","text":"7. Lohse KR, Lang CE, Boyd LA. Is more better? Using metadata to explore dose-response relationships in stroke rehabilitation. Stroke. 2014;45(7):2053-8.","guid":"6B6C4AB74B3B426A8A7DFF7D","children":[]},{"id":"157","parent":"149","text":"8. Trapl M, Enderle P, Nowotny M, et al. Dysphagia bedside screening for acute-stroke patients: the Gugging Swallowing Screen. Stroke. 2007;38(11):2948-52.","guid":"DE2F19111C164E08A9D2BAB1","children":[]}]}]}]},"node_count":157,"relations":[],"cross_references":[],"specialty":"UCI/Medicina Crítica","folder":"Entidades clínicas/UCI-Medicina Crítica","filename":"Manejo de final de vida-2024","id":"map_232","resolved_references":[]}